Will this support a way to configure Bedrock to use AWS profiles without having to hardcode long-term AWS credentials?
As an example, this is what I use for Claude Code (settings.json) and it works fine with temporary credentials (it even supports an auto-refresh mechanism)
```
{
  "awsAuthRefresh": "op account get > /dev/null || eval $(op signin) && aws_mfa.sh -u <my.user> -m $(op item get  'AWS account'  --field type=otp  --format json | jq -r '.[0].totp')",
  "env": {
    "CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK": "1",
    "AWS_PROFILE": "aws-dev",
    "AWS_REGION": "eu-west-1"
  },
  "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6"
}
```
